From: Rohith Chiluka <rchiluka@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] agm: reset ret to 0 after ats thread creation failure

The ATS init thread is optional (guarded by enable_ats_thread).  When
pthread_create() fails for that thread the error code was left in ret,
causing agm_init() to return a failure to its caller even though all
mandatory initialisation had already succeeded.  Clear ret after logging
the error so that a non-fatal ATS thread failure does not propagate.

---
 service/src/agm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/service/src/agm.c b/service/src/agm.c
index 25a38d5..8a2ef27 100644
--- a/service/src/agm.c
+++ b/service/src/agm.c
@@ -164,6 +164,7 @@ int agm_init()
         if (ret) {
             AGM_LOGE("ats init thread creation failed");
             ats_thread_started = false;
+            ret = 0;
         } else {
             ats_thread_started = true;
         }
--
